# Security

Welcome to the Codexeron Security Documentation.

Security is an important part of the Codexeron Marketplace experience.

This section explains general security practices used to help protect buyers, sellers, products, and transactions.

---

# Security Overview

Codexeron focuses on:

- Account security
- Secure transactions
- Product protection
- Data privacy
- Safe marketplace operations

---

# Account Security

Users should protect their accounts by:

- Using strong passwords.
- Keeping login information private.
- Enabling Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) when available.
- Avoiding suspicious links.
- Reviewing account activity.

---

# Payment Security

For safer transactions:

- Use official Codexeron payment instructions.
- Verify transaction details carefully.
- Never share private wallet keys.
- Keep payment records secure.

---

# Product Security

Codexeron encourages developers to provide secure products.

Products should:

- Follow secure coding practices.
- Avoid malicious behavior.
- Protect user data.
- Maintain updated dependencies.

---

# Download Protection

Purchased products may be protected through:

- Account-based access.
- Secure download systems.
- License verification.
- Access control mechanisms.

---

# Data Protection

Codexeron aims to handle user information responsibly.

Security practices may include:

- Protecting account data.
- Limiting unauthorized access.
- Monitoring platform security.
- Improving security systems continuously.

---

# Reporting Security Issues

If you discover a security issue:

Please report it through the official Codexeron support channels.

Security reports should include:

- Issue description
- Affected area
- Steps to reproduce
- Additional technical details when available

---

# Responsible Disclosure

Security researchers and users are encouraged to report vulnerabilities responsibly.

Please avoid:

- Publicly sharing vulnerabilities before resolution.
- Accessing unauthorized data.
- Disrupting marketplace services.

---

# Learn More

For detailed security policies, visit:

https://www.codexeron.com

